"text": "Start with why. These are F-zero-twos, Figure's second-generation humanoid. Figure says they spent months loading parts at a BMW plant. But as its newer F-zero-three fleet grew, keeping the old ones running stopped making sense. So what do you do with a retired robot? Sell it? Figure says they're packed with its own custom hardware, like the actuators that move the joints, and it didn't want that leaving the building. Take them apart? Figure says doing that for every robot would eat so much engineering time, it would delay the next model. Melt them? Simple. Except a robot that jumps in on its own brings its battery along. Figure says foundries in the U.S. and Mexico refused. One in Imatra, Finland, said yes. Recycling old hardware is normal. Bringing a film crew is not.",
